"""Equal inputs/budget/service, assigned frozen Skill and no cross-arm leakage."""
from pathlib import Path
import study as s
R=s.R
T='''Use your assigned native-ui-agent Skill to review and improve this real new dual-platform component PR. Workspace: {workspace}. Assigned read-only Skill: {tool}. Read public independent design: {public}. Original shared D0 evidence: {d0}. Read SESSION.json for actual handoff time and deadline. Fresh context: do not read assignments, other arms/workspaces/tools, old studies, hidden inputs, external judgments or other agent outputs. Do not communicate with other agents. Do not intentionally insert defects, edit design/expected values/units, change tool/framework/host/bridges, or rebuild test UI instead of fixing production code. Write only approved production paths plus own agent-output/cache.

One identical initial production PR and the same D0 raw/automatic evidence are supplied to both conditions. Use your assigned Skill's actual executable capabilities. Both conditions share the same validated optimized native execution service, fixed routes, fixtures, hardware policy and public test information. Pixel/automatic evidence supplied by the common service is available to both. Determine causes from actual source + original images; observation failures are not automatically product defects. Cover all public business obligations and visual states, including remote long content and caller updates. Full-content missing/unknown cannot silently pass.

At most20 wall minutes from SESSION.handoffAtUnix, including review/editing/compile/native waits; early finish allowed. Up to TWO inner native feedback requests, no direct SDK acquisitions/previews/app launch. Use only:
python3 {feedback} --workspace {workspace} [--case P1|P2 repeatable] [--state <approved-state-id> repeatable]
This service seals exact current sources, verifies immutable inputs, queues platform slots, and writes feedback/<unit>/request-N/evidence. It blocks until the actual capture and automatic result; do not edit production source while in flight. In-flight request may drain beyond budget; record overrun and then stop edits. Selected feedback is incomplete; full fresh final runs automatically after your final source seal. You can inspect all your own service evidence and source after requests. Optional compile-only helper is {compile}; its wall time counts. No unlogged native command is authorized.

Immediately create agent-output/phase-start.json actual Unix start. Before first code change, record original findings in agent-output/claims.json as {{findings:[{{id,origin:'manual',status:'failed'|'unassessed'|'passed',platform:'ios'|'android',case:'P1'|'P2',assertion_ids:[original state/rule IDs],reason,snapshot_indices:[original indices],evidence:[original path+SHA refs]}}]}}. Assertions are exact existing independent IDs; outside-index observations retain original prose/evidence and empty assertion_ids rather than inventing expected values. Preserve the first original claims unchanged, write subsequent findings in separate version files referenced from repair.json BEFORE final close; keep claims.json unchanged and do not expand initial scopes using later repair success. Machine failures already in automatic.json need not be rewritten as manual claims. Keep operator/schema mistakes and limitations distinct from product alarms.

Use assigned Skill tools where useful: a requirement route or partial-capture disposition is a decision, not visual truth or automatic product-cause proof. Record root causes, changes and directed verification, avoid churn for unknown measurement capability. End by writing agent-output/repair.json with actual startedAtUnix/finishedAtUnix, changed_files, original finding references, fixes, verified/unverified outcomes, native request refs, unresolved MUSTs, claimed_release_status, and limits/overruns. Retain source versions and every failed attempt.

Then immediately invoke the shared final-close service (outside the editing budget; no further source edits):
python3 {close} --workspace {workspace}
It seals your final source/original findings and starts your own FULL public capture and automatic checks as soon as your slot is available; it does not wait for unrelated units. After it returns, do not edit source or run any more SDK feedback. Inspect your own fresh full final PNGs and complete all public qualitative review actuals through the assigned review_contract tools. Write agent-output/final-self/phase.json with actual review start; per ios/android × P1/P2 write submission.json exactly {{version:1,catalog_sha256:<canonical generated catalog digest>,observation_sha256:<original observation file SHA>,decisions:[{{review_id,actual:true|false|null,reason,snapshot_indices:[]}}]}} under agent-output/final-self/<platform>/<case>. Catalog/review IDs come from the approved plan/lock/policy; the original final observation is {corpus}/<platform>/<case>/native/observation.json. Include every qualitative visual atom; no expected/unit/pixel overrides. Missing evidence remains null. Keep review logs/limits and actual completedAtUnix in phase record. Then call python3 {selfcheck} --workspace {workspace}. It verifies the original full capture and recomputes the final self-check/gate. Full results may remain failed/unverified. This final review/service is outside editing budget but its actual wall time counts in a separate full Skill endpoint; no unrelated-arm barrier is added. Do not inspect external/hidden results or repair after source close. Finish with exact result paths and limitations. No commits/pushes.'''
def prepare(unit):
 cfg=s.read(R/'private/assignment.json')['units'][unit]
 text=T.format(workspace=R/'cache'/unit,tool=R/cfg['tool'],public=R/'design'/cfg['task']/'public',d0=R/'corpora'/cfg['task']/'d0',feedback=R/'feedback.py',compile=R/'compile_only.py',close=R/'close_session.py',corpus=R/'corpora'/unit/'final-public',selfcheck=R/'final_self_check.py')
 s.save(R/'operators'/(unit+'-delivery.json'),{'unit':unit,'preparedAtUnix':__import__('time').time(),'prompt':text})
 return text
if __name__=='__main__':
 import sys;print(prepare(sys.argv[1]))
